{
  "_doc": "Copy to .qa/config.json and edit. Driver presets resolve the browser endpoint: managed (zero-config built-in Playwright, any OS), windows+wsl (attach to Windows Chrome from WSL), windows, wsl, linux, mac. The managed driver is the default; attended CDP is opt-in. apiOrigin is optional — set it only when the backend API is served from a different origin than baseUrl (enables cross-origin probing; leave \"\" for same-origin). repos are all optional (single-repo works); skills read them by role. allowApiWrites is OFF by default — direct API writes/seeding are gated behind it AND a disposable-env marker.",
  "baseUrl": "http://localhost:3000",
  "apiOrigin": "",
  "auth": {
    "storageState": ".qa/auth/storageState.json"
  },
  "drivers": [
    {
      "id": "managed",
      "server": "playwright",
      "preset": "managed"
    },
    {
      "id": "mine",
      "server": "playwright-cdp",
      "preset": "windows+wsl",
      "cdpEndpoint": "http://localhost:9222"
    }
  ],
  "maxParallel": 3,
  "repos": [
    { "role": "frontend", "path": "/home/dev/projects/elevator/pioneer-dashboard" },
    { "role": "backend", "path": "/home/dev/projects/elevator/backend" },
    { "role": "reference", "path": "/home/dev/projects/elevator/governance" }
  ],
  "allowApiWrites": false,
  "seedableEnvMarker": "QA_DISPOSABLE_ENV",
  "_stackDoc": "Stack detection + production safety. environment: 'auto' infers production from a non-localhost baseUrl with no seedableEnvMarker (forces writes off, conservative fingerprint, crawl off); set 'disposable' or 'production' to override. allowBlackboxCrawl: only true lets the agent live-crawl a non-disposable target (else it verifies only checklist-named surfaces). fingerprintPaths: <=4 well-known doc paths probed read-only during detection. noProbePaths: paths never to fetch. crawlDenyPatterns: extra link patterns to skip on a black-box crawl (logout/delete/etc. are always skipped). maxRequestsPerSecond: throttle for fingerprint/crawl GETs.",
  "environment": "auto",
  "allowBlackboxCrawl": false,
  "fingerprintPaths": ["/openapi.json", "/swagger/v1/swagger.json"],
  "noProbePaths": [],
  "crawlDenyPatterns": [],
  "maxRequestsPerSecond": 2,
  "memory": {
    "backend": "file",
    "mem0": {
      "endpoint": "",
      "apiKeyEnv": "MEM0_API_KEY",
      "userId": "qa-e2e-pilot"
    }
  },
  "_viewportDoc": "Viewport, responsive matrix, persona lens, detection, gate knobs, interaction discipline, and isolation (ADR-0008/ADR-0015/ADR-0003). viewport: the desktop size Pre-flight applies via browser_resize before any criterion runs. responsiveMatrix: opt-in extra viewports (e.g. mobile); empty = off (default) — when set, ONLY viewport-sensitive UX criteria (overflow/target-size) re-run per listed viewport, functional criteria are never multiplied. persona.lens: the default review lens (skeptical-auditor | first-time-user | a11y-user) applied on top of the role axis already confirmed in personas[]/authz-matrix.json (role x lens — this key only sets the lens; it never regenerates roles). detection.ux: which UX detector streams run (objective = real fail@FE verdicts; advisoryAesthetics = subjective, reported, never gated). passGate.enforce: whether checkpoint.sh's evidence gate (ADR-0010) rejects an unevidenced pass — leave true; disable only for a temporary, deliberate escape hatch. humanInteraction.enforce: gate human interaction via ADR-0015; audit-only fallback, never silently off. saveSession: default true (Plan H3/B) — enables Check 0 (independent session.md reconciliation) WHEN a session log is present. Check 0 degrades gracefully when it's absent, so flipping this on is safe even if the driver isn't actually logging yet. HONEST CAVEAT: this flag alone does not make Claude capture a session log — Claude has no bundled mcp.snippet, so the operator must still add \"--save-session\" to their own Playwright MCP server args (see driving-browser-qa's pre-flight detection); without that, the gate degrades to the act-lint + fingerprint checks and flags that independent-log verification was unavailable. autonomousSetup: default false (interactive). SETUP PHASES ONLY (decision #8) — when true, confirming-discovered-roles' 3-round HITL (roles/credentials/scope) PROACTIVELY auto-accepts every round's recommendedDefault instead of prompting a human, tagging each accepted item assumption:true — for headless/CI/`/loop` runs where no human is present to answer. This NEVER affects the Verify loop, which already never interrupts; it only changes pre-run setup confirmation. maxOptOutRate: flag a run whose nonUiActionReason rate exceeds it — opt-out-abuse guard. isolation.maxOpenContexts: cap concurrent browser contexts; default = effective concurrency, ~1 under ADR-0003. mechanism: isolated in-memory profile vs user-data-dir; never shared-browser-context for fan-out. Note: allowApiWrites+disposable-marker remain the ONLY write gate — origin lists are not a write boundary. criteriaBudget: soft cap on criteria generated/run in one pass, a cost lever, not a coverage cut.",
  "viewport": { "width": 1440, "height": 900 },
  "responsiveMatrix": [],
  "persona": { "lens": "skeptical-auditor" },
  "detection": {
    "ux": { "objective": true, "advisoryAesthetics": true }
  },
  "passGate": { "enforce": true },
  "fixtures": { "hardBlock": false },
  "humanInteraction": { "enforce": true, "saveSession": true, "autonomousSetup": false, "maxOptOutRate": 0.2, "sessionLogDir": ".playwright-mcp" },
  "enforcement": {
    "_doc": "Layer 1 (record) of the out-of-agent evidence enforcement (ADR-0018/Plan H2). captureHook: whether the PostToolUse capture-hook (scripts/capture-hook.sh) is active; it always no-ops safely when false or when there's no active run, never errors the tool call either way. secretPatterns: POSIX-ERE-compatible regexes (no lookaround/backreferences -- matched via jq's built-in regex or python3 're', never grep -P/perl) tested case-insensitively against every string in a captured Bash call's args AND tool_response (stdout/stderr); any match is replaced with \"<redacted>\" before the line is written. FAIL-SAFE DEFAULT (security-critical): if this `secretPatterns` key is ABSENT -- including when the whole `enforcement` block is absent -- a hard-coded built-in default pattern list applies (password, passwd, secret, token, api[_-]?key, apikey, authorization, bearer, access[_-]?key, private[_-]?key, client[_-]?secret; see scripts/toolstream.sh's DEFAULT_SECRET_PATTERNS_JSON). An explicit `\"secretPatterns\": []` is different from absent: it means the operator has deliberately OPTED OUT of pattern-based redaction, and that empty set is honored as-is (redactedKeys literal-substring redaction still applies). redactedKeys: literal declared credential VALUES (not regexes) to redact the same way, wherever they appear as a substring. Bash tool_response is redacted with the SAME pass as Bash args (a command's OUTPUT -- `env`, `cat .env`, `echo $API_KEY`, `curl -v` echoing an Authorization header -- can leak a secret as easily as its arguments). browser_* args (and non-Bash tool_response) are captured in FULL (test data) -- a browser_type into a password field can still capture a typed secret; that's a documented residual, not silently claimed safe.",
    "captureHook": true,
    "secretPatterns": ["(?i)(password|token|secret|api[_-]?key)\\s*[=:]\\s*\\S+"],
    "redactedKeys": []
  },
  "isolation": { "maxOpenContexts": 1, "mechanism": "isolated" },
  "criteriaBudget": 60
}
